    <string name="install_icons" formatted="false">Set up your icons</string>
    <string name="install_icons_1" formatted="false">Export the icon pack and save the folder to Files. Choose the image for the app you want to customize.</string>
    <string name="install_icons_2" formatted="false">In Shortcuts, create an Open App action and choose the app. Open its menu and select Add to Home Screen.</string>
    <string name="install_icons_3" formatted="false">Tap the icon, choose your saved image and give it a name. Tap Add. Repeat for your other apps; original app icons are unchanged.</string>
    <string name="install_intro" formatted="false">A few steps. A whole new look.</string>
    <string name="install_manual" formatted="false">iOS handles the final setup. Tap each step when you\'ve completed it; we\'ll remember your progress.</string>
    <string name="install_mark" formatted="false">Tap when done</string>
    <string name="install_title" formatted="false">Set it up</string>
    <string name="install_wallpaper" formatted="false">Set your wallpaper</string>
    <string name="install_wallpaper_1" formatted="false">Open Settings → Wallpaper → Add New Wallpaper. Choose Photos and select the image you saved.</string>
    <string name="install_wallpaper_2" formatted="false">For a Live Photo, enable motion if iOS offers it. For an eligible image, try Spatial Scene. Adjust the crop and clock in the system editor.</string>
    <string name="install_wallpaper_3" formatted="false">Tap Add, then choose Set as Wallpaper Pair or customize your Home Screen. Wake your phone to check the result.</string>
    <string name="install_widgets" formatted="false">Add your widgets</string>
    <string name="install_widgets_1" formatted="false">Choose your widget background in ScreenMotion. On the Home Screen, touch and hold an empty area.</string>
    <string name="install_widgets_2" formatted="false">Tap Edit → Add Widget, find ScreenMotion, choose a size and tap Add Widget. On older iOS versions, use the + button.</string>
    <string name="install_widgets_3" formatted="false">Touch and hold the widget → Edit Widget to choose Photo, Clock &amp; Date, Calendar or Collection. Lock Screen widgets are added in the system Lock Screen editor.</string>
